{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"32a93d593c1992b556b3bac42ba9921cccbf1fee"},"timestamp":1511961477,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzc3NTA5NDI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2004","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad create-sibling-github interactive configuration does not support 2FA","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nI set up two factor authentication (as everybody should! ;)), and the interactive configuration of `datalad create-sibling-github` doesn't work. Also the suggested method in the manpage (using https://github.com/sociomantic/git-hub) fails, because they do not support 2FA yet. The solution is to create manually a personal access token here: https://github.com/settings/tokens/new. \n\nI can update the manpage if desired.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n\n```terminal\ncontematto@head1 /data/famface/openfmri/data (master) $ datalad create-sibling-github famface_data\nYou need to authenticate with 'github' credentials. https://github.com/login provides information on how to gain access\nuser: mvdoc\n\npassword:\npassword (repeat):\n[ERROR  ] 401 {'message': 'Must specify two-factor authentication OTP code.', 'documentation_url': 'https://developer.github.com/v3/auth#working-with-two-factor-authentication'} [Requester.py:__check:180] (TwoFactorException)\n```","files":null}]}